# 103 (found 2026-10-07 loading remotes/ into the suite harness, G12
# phase 10), by design in the language, whose consequence is the
# finding: JSON Schema reads a definition that admits nothing as a
# schema like any other, which a document may hold and never use, and
# the import writes every $defs entry as an alias declaration. A
# declaration whose value admits nothing is a conflict wherever it is
# used, as docs/design/ALIASES.0.md has it, so vet refuses every
# instance. This is the import of
#   {"$defs": {"A": {"allOf": [{"type": "number"}, {"type": "string"}]}},
#    "type": "string"}
# and both ports agree.
#
# expected: {"schema":"a"}
# actual:   [aontu/empty_domain] at $.%A
%A = number & empty()
schema: empty()
schema: "a"
